\pard\qc\b\fs36 GuruBramha Platform - Database Documentation\b0\fs24\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\par\b\fs32 1. Database Overview\b0\fs24\par
- \\b Database Name\\b0 : GuruBramha (Configurable via "MONGODB_URI")\par
- \\b Purpose of the database\\b0 : To securely manage and persist all platform data including user identities, elite course content, practice arena challenges, interview preparation roadmaps, transaction histories, and verified DigiLocker documents.\par
- \\b Technologies used\\b0 : MongoDB (NoSQL Database), Mongoose (Node.js ODM)\par
- \\b Connection structure\\b0 : The application connects to a MongoDB cluster using a secure connection string defined in the environment variables. The connection is established in "server/index.js" using "mongoose.connect()".\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 2. Complete Collections Structure\b0\fs24\par
\par\b\fs28 2.1 Users Collection (`users`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores user identities, academic profiles, external portfolio links, and subscription details.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key, Auto-generated)\par
  - "firebaseUid": String (Required, Unique, Indexed)\par
  - "displayName": String (Required)\par
  - "email": String (Required, Unique, Indexed)\par
  - "photoURL", "phone", "gender", "college", "branch", "academicYear", "district", "state", "postalCode": String (Optional)\par
  - "age": Number (Optional)\par
  - "githubUrl", "leetcodeUrl", "codechefUrl": String (Optional)\par
  - "isSubscribed": Boolean (Default: "false")\par
  - "subscriptionEndDate": Date (Optional)\par
  - "scholarPoints": Number (Default: "0")\par
  - "currentStreak": Number (Default: "0")\par
  - "solvedProblems": Array of ObjectIds (Ref: "Problem")\par
  - "bookmarkedCompanies": Array of ObjectIds (Ref: "Company")\par
  - "createdAt", "updatedAt": Date (Auto-generated)\par
\par\b\fs28 2.2 Courses Collection (`courses`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores details for the elite course library and curriculum.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key)\par
  - "title": String (Required)\par
  - "instructor": String (Required)\par
  - "category": String (Required)\par
  - "level": String (Required, Enum: "Beginner", "Intermediate", "Advanced")\par
  - "price": Number (Required)\par
  - "originalPrice": Number (Optional)\par
  - "duration": String (Optional)\par
  - "rating", "reviewsCount", "studentsEnrolled": Number (Default: "0")\par
  - "thumbnail", "description": String (Optional)\par
  - "lessons": Array of Objects:\par
    - "title" (String, Required)\par
    - "duration", "videoUrl" (String, Optional)\par
    - "isFreePreview" (Boolean, Default: "false")\par
\par\b\fs28 2.3 Problems Collection (`problems`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores coding challenges for the Elite Practice Arena.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key)\par
  - "title": String (Required)\par
  - "difficulty": String (Required, Enum: "Easy", "Medium", "Hard")\par
  - "category": String (Required)\par
  - "description": String (Required)\par
  - "tags": Array of Strings\par
  - "accuracy": Number (Default: "0")\par
  - "points": Number (Default: "100")\par
  - "validationCases": Array of Objects:\par
    - "input", "output" (String)\par
    - "isHidden" (Boolean, Default: "false")\par
\par\b\fs28 2.4 Companies Collection (`companies`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores interview preparation roadmaps and placement protocols.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key)\par
  - "name": String (Required)\par
  - "type": String (Required, Enum: "Product Based", "Service Based", "Startup")\par
  - "difficulty": String (Enum: "Easy", "Medium", "Hard", "Expert")\par
  - "logo", "package", "overview", "eligibility": String (Optional)\par
  - "skills", "process": Array of Strings\par
  - "rounds": Array of Objects ("title" String, "topics" Array of Strings)\par
  - "roadmap30Days": Array of Objects ("week" Number, "focus" String)\par
\par\b\fs28 2.5 Transactions Collection (`transactions`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores Razorpay payment and subscription details.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key)\par
  - "user": ObjectId (Required, Foreign Key -> "User")\par
  - "amount": Number (Required)\par
  - "currency": String (Default: "INR")\par
  - "razorpayOrderId": String (Required, Indexed)\par
  - "razorpayPaymentId", "razorpaySignature", "receipt": String (Optional)\par
  - "status": String (Enum: "created", "successful", "failed", Default: "created")\par
\par\b\fs28 2.6 Documents Collection (`documents`)\b0\fs24\par
Stores metadata for certificates fetched via DigiLocker.\par
- \\b Fields & Data Types\\b0 :\par
  - "_id": ObjectId (Primary Key)\par
  - "user": ObjectId (Required, Foreign Key -> "User")\par
  - "digilockerId": String (Required)\par
  - "name", "uri": String (Required)\par
  - "type": String (Optional)\par
  - "issueDate": Date (Optional)\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 3. User Side Database Structure\b0\fs24\par
From the user's perspective, the database structure facilitates the following:\par
- \\b Authentication/Login\\b0 : Managed via Firebase on the frontend, which syncs with the "users" collection using the "firebaseUid".\par
- \\b Profile Data\\b0 : Users can update their academic history, age, gender, and social links (GitHub, LeetCode) directly into the "users" table.\par
- \\b Courses\\b0 : Users browse the "courses" collection. Premium courses check the "user.isSubscribed" flag before granting access to video URLs.\par
- \\b Subscriptions & Payments\\b0 : Initiating a purchase creates a "transaction" document. Upon success via Razorpay, the "user.isSubscribed" flag is set to "true" and the "subscriptionEndDate" is extended.\par
- \\b Practice/Coding\\b0 : Users query the "problems" collection. Successful submissions append the Problem's ObjectId to "user.solvedProblems" and increase "user.scholarPoints".\par
- \\b Documents\\b0 : Users authenticating with DigiLocker create records in the "documents" collection, linking official certificates to their profile via the "user" foreign key.\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 4. Admin Side Database Structure\b0\fs24\par
The admin perspective provides full control over the platform's content and tracking:\par
- \\b User Management\\b0 : Admins can query the "users" collection to monitor "scholarPoints", view academic demographics, or manually revoke/grant subscriptions ("isSubscribed").\par
- \\b Content Management\\b0 : Admins have CRUD access to "courses", "problems", and "companies". They can add new coding challenges, update curriculum videos, and add new interview roadmaps.\par
- \\b Transactions & Reports\\b0 : Admins query the "transactions" collection filtered by "status: 'successful'" to generate revenue reports and track active subscriptions.\par
- \\b Analytics\\b0 : Aggregating "user.solvedProblems", "course.studentsEnrolled", and "problem.accuracy" helps admins track platform engagement.\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 5. Flow Charts\b0\fs24\par
""`mermaid\par
graph TD\par
    %% User Registration / Login Flow\par
    subgraph Registration & Login\par
    A1[User opens App] --> A2\{Has Account?\}\par
    A2 -- No --> A3[Firebase Signup]\par
    A3 --> A4[Backend creates Document in 'Users' Collection]\par
    A2 -- Yes --> A5[Firebase Login]\par
    A5 --> A6[Backend fetches 'Users' Document]\par
    end\par
    %% Course Purchase & Subscription Flow\par
    subgraph Payment & Subscription\par
    B1[User clicks Buy Subscription] --> B2[Backend creates Razorpay Order]\par
    B2 --> B3[Create pending record in 'Transactions' Collection]\par
    B3 --> B4[User completes Payment via Razorpay UI]\par
    B4 --> B5[Backend verifies Signature /verify route]\par
    B5 --> B6[Update Transaction status to 'successful']\par
    B6 --> B7[Update User 'isSubscribed' to true]\par
    end\par
    %% Document Upload / DigiLocker Flow\par
    subgraph DigiLocker Flow\par
    C1[User clicks Link DigiLocker] --> C2[Redirect to DigiLocker OAuth]\par
    C2 --> C3[User Approves Access]\par
    C3 --> C4[Backend receives Callback Code]\par
    C4 --> C5[Backend exchanges Code for Access Token]\par
    C5 --> C6[Fetch Issued Documents]\par
    C6 --> C7[Save metadata to 'Documents' Collection]\par
    end\par
""`\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 6. API & Backend Mapping\b0\fs24\par
The frontend communicates with the MongoDB collections via the following expected REST API mapping:\par
- \\b Authentication / Profile\\b0 \par
  - "POST /api/auth/sync" -> Maps to "User.findOneOrCreate()"\par
  - "GET /api/users/profile" -> Maps to "User.findById()"\par
  - "PUT /api/users/profile" -> Maps to "User.findByIdAndUpdate()"\par
- \\b Courses\\b0 \par
  - "GET /api/courses" -> Maps to "Course.find()"\par
  - "GET /api/courses/:id" -> Maps to "Course.findById()" (Protected payload checks "User.isSubscribed")\par
- \\b Practice Arena\\b0 \par
  - "GET /api/problems" -> Maps to "Problem.find()"\par
  - "POST /api/problems/:id/submit" -> Verifies code, updates "User.solvedProblems" & "User.scholarPoints"\par
- \\b Interview Roadmaps\\b0 \par
  - "GET /api/companies" -> Maps to "Company.find()"\par
  - "POST /api/companies/:id/bookmark" -> Updates "User.bookmarkedCompanies"\par
- \\b Payments ("/api/payment")\\b0 \par
  - "POST /order" -> Uses Razorpay API, creates "Transaction" doc\par
  - "POST /verify" -> Verifies signature, updates "Transaction" status, updates "User" subscription\par
- \\b DigiLocker ("/api/digilocker")\\b0 \par
  - "GET /authorize" -> Redirects to Gov portal\par
  - "GET /callback" -> Processes OAuth token\par
  - "GET /documents" -> Fetches external API, saves to "Documents"\par
\par --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par\b\fs32 7. Deployment Readiness\b0\fs24\par
\par\b\fs28 Environment Variables Required (`.env` file)\b0\fs24\par
""`env\par
PORT=5000\par
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster.mongodb.net/gurubramha?retryWrites=true&w=majority\par
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend-domain.com\par
\pard\qc\b\fs36 Razorpay Keys\b0\fs24\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_key_id\par
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_key_secret\par
\pard\qc\b\fs36 DigiLocker Keys\b0\fs24\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id\par
DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret\par
DIGILOCKER_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5000/api/digilocker/callback\par
\pard\qc\b\fs36 Firebase Admin SDK\b0\fs24\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id\par
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\n...\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\n"\par
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=your_client_email\par
""`\par
\par\b\fs28 Database Setup Instructions\b0\fs24\par
1. Create a MongoDB Atlas cluster or install MongoDB locally.\par
2. Obtain the connection string and insert it into "MONGODB_URI".\par
3. In "index.js", the database connects automatically.\par
4. (Optional) Create a seed script using Mongoose to insert initial courses and problems into the collections.\par
\par\b\fs28 Production-Ready Checks & Security\b0\fs24\par
- \\b Network Security\\b0 : Ensure MongoDB Atlas Network Access is IP-restricted (e.g., only Azure server IP allowed).\par
- \\b CORS\\b0 : The "cors" configuration in "index.js" correctly restricts origins to trusted frontend domains.\par
- \\b Environment Secrets\\b0 : Ensure ".env" is listed in ".gitignore" and keys are managed securely in Azure/Vercel secrets.\par
- \\b Indexes\\b0 : Mongoose schemas have implicit indexes (e.g., "unique: true" on emails), ensuring fast queries.\par
- \\b Validation\\b0 : Mongoose enforces schema validation (Required fields, Enums, Number formats) preventing malformed data entry from API requests.\par
